                <pb facs="0135" n="31" xml:id="pg31"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mizner to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">El Paso, Tex.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1890-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            8, 1890</date>. (Received July 10.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Mizner reports that serious troubles between the Government of Guatemala and
                    Salvadorian provisional leaders exist; that armies of 10,000 are prepared for
                    battle in either state, and that the presence of a United States naval vessel on
                    the Pacific coast of Central America is necessary for the protection of our
                    interests in those states.</p>
            </div>
